{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And to the woman He said, etc.</b> R. Solomon son of R. Moses explained: that she shall be in pain and toil all her days. And if you ask: what do I care? I have many maidservants to serve me — Scripture says: והרונך — against your will you will be pregnant. And if you ask: I will give birth at leisure — Scripture says: בעצב תלדי בנים. And if you ask: I will guard myself from having relations with my husband — Scripture says: ואל אישך תשוקתך. And if you ask: I will suppress my desire and not have relations with him — Scripture says: והוא ימשל בך — against your will you will have relations with him." "<b>And he shall rule over you.</b> We say in Bereshit Rabbah: I might think rule from every side — Scripture says: לא יחבול ריחים ורכב. And R. Yitzchak explained: I might think rule from every side, that he would have authority to pledge his wife as security — Scripture says: לא יחבול ריחים ורכב. And a woman is called ריחים, as it is written: ויהי טוחן בבית האסורים, as expounded in Sotah, and as it is written: תטחן לאחר אשתי. And in the Yerushalmi, this verse was translated: לא תמשכנון ריחיא ורכבא, ארי צרכי נפשאתא אינון, ולא תאסור כליין וחתנין, ארום כל דעבד אלין, כמה דכפר בעלמא דאתי. And he explained: לא תאסור כליין וחתנין — that if he betroths a woman, he must not leave her sitting abandoned in betrothal for a long time."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:04.800138740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}